#cheatsheet-box(title: "Master Strategy Cheatsheet — Social Histories & Mahabharata")[
  - *Textual Dichotomy:* Never treat prescriptive texts (*Dharmasutras*, *Manusmriti*) as actual social descriptions. Always look for epigraphic counter-evidence (e.g., Satavahana gotra practices, Prabhavati Gupta land grant).
  - *Gotra Exogamy vs Endogamy:* Brahmanical rule = strict *exogamy* (marry outside gotra). Satavahana practice = royal *endogamy* (marrying within same gotra / cross-cousins).
  - *Varna vs Jati:* Varnas are rigidly fixed at *4* (Brahmana, Kshatriya, Vaishya, Shudra). Jatis are *unlimited* and accommodated occupational guilds, tribes, and foreign immigrants.
  - *Stridhana vs Patrimony:* Sons inherited immovable land and cattle (*patrimony*); women could not inherit family land, but retained personal ownership over wedding gifts (*Stridhana*).
  - *Authorship Layers:* The core epic was originally composed by *sutas* (charioteer-bards), then written down by *Brahmanas* (c. 5th c. BCE), and expanded with Vaishnava didactic sections (c. 200 BCE – 400 CE) attributed to *Vyasa*.
]

#exception-box(title: "The Seven Fatal CUET Traps")[
  1. *Trap 1 (Duration of Critical Edition):* Confusing 47 years with 25 or 50 years. Project began in *1919* and ended in *1966* (*47 years*).
  2. *Trap 2 (Satavahana Matriliny Myth):* Assuming Satavahanas were matrilineal because of matronymics. Royal succession was strictly *patrilineal* (son succeeded father).
  3. *Trap 3 (Draupadi's Polyandry Generalization):* Assuming polyandry was the standard practice. It was rare and exceptional; patrilineal exogamy was the Brahmanical norm.
  4. *Trap 4 (Ekalavya's Caste):* Stigmatizing Ekalavya as a Shudra. He was a *Nishada* (forest-dwelling hunter-gatherer), outside the varna system entirely.
  5. *Trap 5 (Mandasor Guild Identification):* Confusing the Mandasor inscription with ivory carvers of Vidisha. Mandasor relates to *silk weavers* from Lata (Gujarat).
  6. *Trap 6 (Buddhist Social Contract Authority):* Attaching divine sanction to Mahasammata. He was chosen by *human consensus* (*social contract*), not divine ordination.
  7. *Trap 7 (Hastinapura Archaeologist):* Mixing up B.B. Lal with John Marshall or Alexander Cunningham. *B.B. Lal* excavated Hastinapura in *1951–1952*.
]

